From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 21:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/edid: demote zero block message to debug

Some displays and adapters return an all-zero EDID while the DRM connector
polls for a display.  The notice is then emitted on every poll and floods the
kernel log without providing actionable information.

Keep the diagnostic available at debug level.  Other EDID corruption notices
remain unchanged.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_edid.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_edid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_edid.c
@@ -1927,7 +1927,7 @@
 		pr_debug("EDID block %d pointer is NULL\n", block_num);
 		break;
 	case EDID_BLOCK_ZERO:
-		pr_notice("EDID block %d is all zeroes\n", block_num);
+		pr_debug("EDID block %d is all zeroes\n", block_num);
 		break;
 	case EDID_BLOCK_HEADER_CORRUPT:
 		pr_notice("EDID has corrupt header\n");
